/**
\defgroup input Input
\brief Named input actions. You declare an action, bind keys to it (on press, while held, or on release), and read its value from your systems.

<table class="markdownTable">
<tr><td><b>Source</b></td><td>\srcdir{include/Input} · \srcdir{src/Input}</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Include</b></td><td>`#include <Input/Module.hpp>`</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Namespaces</b></td><td>`Input`; your actions live in `Input::Actions`</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Started by</b></td><td>Nothing to start: `Input::Module()` is empty. Engine::Run() calls Input::UpdateInputs() every frame.</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Examples</b></td><td>\ref ex_input · \ref ex_movement · every game</td></tr>
</table>

## How to use

<b>1. Declare an action</b> at global scope with #DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION: a name and the type of value it produces. It becomes `Input::Actions::<Name>`.

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Declaring actions}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp actions
\endex

<b>2. Bind keys</b> with `AddInputBindings_Press`, `AddInputBindings_Hold` or `AddInputBindings_Release`. Each binding is a key (an `SDL_Scancode`) and the value it contributes:

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Binding keys}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp bindings
\endex

<b>3. Read the action</b> in a system. Input is read at the start of each frame, before systems run:

| Call | Returns |
| --- | --- |
| `Input::IsActionTriggered(Input::Actions::Jump)` | `true` if any of its bindings triggered this frame |
| `Input::GetValue(Input::Actions::Move)` | The combined value of the bindings that triggered (see *Values and operators*) |

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Polling actions in a system}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp polling
\endex

<b>Or register a callback</b> that runs when the action triggers:

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,A callback}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp callback
\endex

## When a binding triggers

| Binding type | Triggers on | Typical use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `PRESS` | The frame the key goes down, **and** every keyboard auto-repeat while it is held | Jump, confirm, toggle |
| `HOLD` | Every frame the key is down | Movement, charging |
| `RELEASE` | The frame the key comes up | Release a charged attack |

Keys are SDL scancodes: physical key positions, named after a US keyboard. `SDL_SCANCODE_W` is the key in W's position on any layout. The full list is in [SDL_scancode.h](https://wiki.libsdl.org/SDL3/SDL_Scancode).

A binding can list several keys. For a `HOLD` binding all of them must be down, which makes key combinations:

```cpp
Input::AddInputBindings_Hold(&Input::Actions::Save, {
    Input::SInputBinding<bool>({SDL_SCANCODE_LCTRL, SDL_SCANCODE_S}, true),
});
```

For `PRESS` and `RELEASE` bindings, multi-key combinations never trigger (\src{src/Input/Module.cpp,65,98}). Use one key per binding.

## Values and operators

`GetValue` starts from a zero value (`TValueType{}`) and applies the value of every triggered binding, in the order they were added, using the action's operator (\src{include/Input/Module.hpp,71,81}):

| Operator | Result | Declare with |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `ADD` (default) | Sum of the triggered bindings' values. Arrow keys `(0,-1)` + `(1,0)` give `(1,-1)`. | `DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION(Name, Type)` |
| `OVERRIDE` | The value of the last triggered binding. Zero if none. | `DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION_WITH_PARAMS(Name, Type, OVERRIDE)` |
| `SUBTRACT` | Zero minus each triggered value | `..._WITH_PARAMS(Name, Type, SUBTRACT)` |
| `MULTIPLY`, `DIVIDE` | Always zero, because they start from zero | — |

Any type that supports `+=` and can be zero-initialized works: `bool`, `float`, `int`, `glm::vec2`, ... For `bool` actions use Input::IsActionTriggered(); `GetValue` on a `bool` action works but makes MSVC warn (C4804).

## Actions the engine declares

| Action | Type | Declared in | Used by |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Input::Actions::Move2D` | `glm::vec2` | \src{include/Gameplay/Module.hpp,12} | Nothing in the engine; ProtoRPG and \ref ex_collision use it for movement |
| `Input::Actions::ToggleDebugColliders` | `bool` | \src{include/Types/Module.hpp,6} | Meant to toggle CoreTypes::bShouldDisplayDebugColliders; your game does the toggling |

The engine binds no keys to them.

## Quitting

Input::UpdateInputs() sets the quit flag when SDL reports a quit event (closing the window), and Engine::Run() then stops. To quit from your own code, push that event:

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Quit on Escape}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp quit
\endex

## Things to watch out for

- **Keyboard only.** Gamepad buttons can be added to bindings, but they are never checked (\src{src/Input/Module.cpp,100,122}).
- **Typing in an ImGui text field also triggers game actions.** The engine passes events to ImGui but does not check whether ImGui wants the keyboard (\src{src/Input/Module.cpp,44}).
- **Register one callback per action.** Each callback runs once for every callback registered on the same action: with two callbacks, both run twice (\src{include/Input/Module.hpp,96,107}).
- Callbacks are checked every frame for every registered callback, triggered or not.
- `PRESS` repeats while the key is held (operating-system key repeat). Track the previous state yourself if you need exactly one trigger per press.
*/

/**
\def DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION(InActionName, ValueType)
\ingroup input
\brief Declares `Input::Actions::InActionName`, an Input::SAction<ValueType> whose bindings' values are added up (`ADD`).

Use at global scope, in one source file or in a header shared by several. Defined at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,103}.

\genexopen{modules/Input.cpp,Actions}
\snippet modules/Input.cpp actions
\endex
*/

/**
\def DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION_WITH_PARAMS(InActionName, ValueType, Operator)
\ingroup input
\brief Like #DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION, with a chosen Input::EInputModifierOperation (`OVERRIDE`, `ADD`, `SUBTRACT`, ...).

Defined at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,98,101}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> void Input::AddInputBindings_Press(SAction<TValueType>* Action, std::initializer_list<SInputBinding<TValueType>> InputBindings)
\ingroup input
\brief Adds bindings that trigger on the frame their key goes down (and on key repeat).

\param Action The action, e.g. `&Input::Actions::Jump`.
\param InputBindings `{ {SDL_SCANCODE_SPACE, value}, ... }`.

Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,34,37}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> void Input::AddInputBindings_Hold(SAction<TValueType>* Action, std::initializer_list<SInputBinding<TValueType>> InputBindings)
\ingroup input
\brief Adds bindings that trigger every frame their key (or all their keys) are held down. Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,44,47}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> void Input::AddInputBindings_Release(SAction<TValueType>* Action, std::initializer_list<SInputBinding<TValueType>> InputBindings)
\ingroup input
\brief Adds bindings that trigger on the frame their key comes up. Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,39,42}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> void Input::AddInputBindings(SAction<TValueType>* Action, const EInputType& InputType, std::initializer_list<SInputBinding<TValueType>> InputBindings)
\ingroup input
\brief Adds bindings of the given Input::EInputType. The `_Press`, `_Hold` and `_Release` versions call this. Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,23,32}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TActionValue> TActionValue Input::GetValue(const SAction<TActionValue>& Action)
\ingroup input
\brief Returns the action's value this frame: its triggered bindings' values combined with its operator, starting from zero.

Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,71,81}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> bool Input::IsActionTriggered(const SAction<TValueType>& Action)
\ingroup input
\brief Returns `true` if any of the action's bindings triggered this frame. Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,83,92}.
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TValueType> void Input::RegisterActionCallback(SAction<TValueType>* Action, const std::function<void(const TValueType&)>& Function)
\ingroup input
\brief Calls `Function` with the action's value on every frame the action triggers, during Input::UpdateInputs().

Register at most one callback per action (see \ref input). Defined at \src{include/Input/Module.hpp,96,107}.
*/

/**
\fn void Input::UpdateInputs()
\ingroup input
\brief Reads this frame's SDL events, records pressed and released keys, passes events to ImGui and runs action callbacks. Engine::Run() calls it every frame.

Defined at \src{src/Input/Module.cpp,35,63}.
*/

/**
\fn bool Input::ShouldQuit()
\ingroup input
\brief `true` once SDL has reported a quit event. Engine::Run() stops when it is. Defined at \src{src/Input/Module.cpp,31,33}.
*/

/**
\fn bool Input::IsBindingTriggered(const SInputBindingBase& Binding)
\ingroup input
\brief Returns `true` if one binding triggered this frame. Used by Input::GetValue() and Input::IsActionTriggered(). Defined at \src{src/Input/Module.cpp,100,122}.
*/

/**
\fn void Input::DispatchTriggeredActions()
\ingroup input
\brief Runs the callbacks registered with Input::RegisterActionCallback(). Called by Input::UpdateInputs().
*/

/**
\fn void Input::AddInputBoundFunction(const std::function<void()>& Func)
\ingroup input
\brief Adds a function that Input::DispatchTriggeredActions() calls every frame. Used by Input::RegisterActionCallback().
*/

/**
\fn template<typename TActionValue> void Input::ApplyBindingOperation(TActionValue* CurrentValue, const TActionValue& NewValue, const EInputModifierOperation& Operation)
\ingroup input
\brief Combines one binding's value into the running value. Used by Input::GetValue().
*/

/**
\fn void Input::Module()
\ingroup input
\brief Empty. The engine does not call it.
*/

/**
\fn void Input::TeardownModule()
\ingroup input
\brief Empty. The engine does not call it.
*/

/**
\struct Input::SAction
\ingroup input
\brief An input action: a name, its bindings, its callbacks and the operator that combines binding values. Create them with #DEFINE_INPUT_ACTION.

Declared at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,76,89}.
*/

/**
\struct Input::SInputBinding
\ingroup input
\brief One binding: the key(s) that trigger it, when (Input::EInputType) and the value it contributes.

Usually written as `{SDL_SCANCODE_W, value}` inside the list passed to `AddInputBindings_*`. For `bool` actions the value can be left out: `SInputBinding<bool>(SDL_SCANCODE_SPACE)`. Declared at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,47,74}.
*/

/**
\struct Input::SInputBindingBase
\ingroup input
\brief The part of a binding that does not depend on the value type: binding type, keyboard keys and (unused) gamepad buttons.
*/

/**
\enum Input::EInputType
\ingroup input
\brief When a binding triggers: `PRESS`, `HOLD` or `RELEASE`. `NONE` never triggers. Declared at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,19,24}.
*/

/**
\enum Input::EInputModifierOperation
\ingroup input
\brief How an action combines its triggered bindings' values. See \ref input. Declared at \src{include/Input/InputTypes.hpp,26,32}.
*/

/**
\typedef Input::ActionNameID
\ingroup input
\brief An action's name (`std::string`).
*/
